     "explanation": "Both concurrent and retrospective review are fully compliant CDI practices. The reason concurrent review dominates is practical: a physician queried while the patient is still admitted has a fresh memory of the case and the documentation still has a functional purpose in guiding ongoing care, so response rates are far higher. Retrospective review remains useful as a quality-assurance safety net, not because concurrent review skips physician involvement.",
