     "explanation": "An EF of 38% falls at or below the 40% threshold for HFrEF (Heart Failure with reduced Ejection Fraction), which corresponds to the ICD-10-CM 'systolic' heart failure category (I50.2-). HFpEF requires EF ≥50%, and HFmrEF covers the 41-49% range — neither applies here.",
