     "explanation": "An agreement rate consistently above roughly 90-95% is a classic warning sign of leading queries — ones that suggest the diagnosis rather than presenting indicators and open options. The correct response is a compliance audit of a query sample, not celebration, benchmark manipulation, or an unrelated productivity change. This mirrors real ACDIS/AHIMA compliance guidance on query quality monitoring.",
